.TH HOME-AUDIT 1 "2026-10-13" "SASD Freeware" "Unix Administration"
.SH NAME
home-audit \- Check local or NSS-enumerated user home-directory metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhome-audit\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks only the home-directory inode and never follows a home symbolic link. Findings do not by themselves imply compromise. Uses local passwd files by default on Linux and NSS enumeration by default on macOS. NSS enumeration is not guaranteed exhaustive; APFS ACLs are not checked.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --source local|nss
Select local passwd text or host NSS enumeration. Explicit --file selects local; --file and --source nss cannot be combined.
.TP
.B --file PATH
Read the specified passwd-style file.
.TP
.B --min-uid N, --max-uid N
Default range is 500 through 59999 on macOS, 1000 through 59999 elsewhere.
.TP
.B --all
Include every enumerated identity.
.TP
.B --null
Emit NUL-separated ISSUE, USER, UID, HOME records.
.TP
.B --help
Display usage information.
.TP
.B --version
Display program version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 completed, 1 malformed local data or traversal errors, 2 argument errors, 3 missing prerequisites.
.SH SEE ALSO
passwd(5), group(5), getent(1)
.SH AUTHOR
SASD Freeware contributors.
